# Path-scoped review ownership for the tenant registry.
#
# Phase 5's gate. Every tenant file's header has said since Phase 0 that writes
# here would be gated by path-scoped CODEOWNERS; this is that file. The write
# path (src/agents/platform/registry_write.py) already refuses to touch more than
# one tenant file — this is the second half, enforced by review rather than code:
# a PR that edits acme's registry entry needs acme's owners.
#
# ⚠️ WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT DO. CODEOWNERS only requests reviewers. It blocks
# nothing until branch protection on `main` requires review from code owners, and
# nothing in this repo does that today. Written down here rather than left to be
# discovered: this file is a routing rule, not an enforcement mechanism, until
# that setting is turned on.
#
# The teams below do not exist yet either. GitHub silently ignores an owner it
# cannot resolve — which means a mis-typed team name looks exactly like a working
# rule. Verify with a test PR before believing it.

# The shared catalog defines capabilities for every tenant; a change here is a
# platform change, not a tenant one.
/platform/catalog.yaml          @men16922

# One rule per tenant, matching one file per tenant. This is the shape the
# registry layout was chosen for.
/platform/tenants/acme.yaml     @men16922
/platform/tenants/globex.yaml   @men16922

# The write path and its guards. Loosening these is how the one-file invariant
# would stop being true without any tenant file appearing in the diff.
/src/agents/platform/registry_write.py   @men16922
/tests/test_registry_write.py            @men16922
/.github/CODEOWNERS                       @men16922
